cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TinyACE-Nepali: Test-Time Context Adaptation for Small Language Models on a Low-Resource Language"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shahi
    given-names: Suryodaya
  - name: Sathwik
  - name: Archit
repository-code: "https://github.com/SirAlchemist1/edge-slm-ace"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
abstract: >-
  Whether a small language model can improve at a task without weight updates,
  by accumulating a playbook of strategies it writes for itself -- and whether
  that still holds in a low-resource language. The playbook is built on an
  adaptation split, frozen, and then evaluated as a static prompt prefix through
  a stock lm-evaluation-harness run on parallel English and Nepali Belebele.
keywords:
  - small language models
  - low-resource languages
  - Nepali
  - context engineering
  - agentic memory
  - test-time adaptation
